    <h1 class="title">Tripartite Agreement</h1>

    <p>This agreement is executed on this ______day of ________________, 2026 Between</p>

    <p><b>SRI. SHAILESH MADHUKAR PACHBHAI S/O. SRI. MADHUKAR PACHBHAI</b>, aged about 36 years, Occupation: Private Employee, Resident of Villa 15, Crown Imperial, Panchaheel Enclave, Bolaram, Secundrabad, hyderabad-500010. (AADHAAR NO. 3523 0722 4815 &amp; PAN NO. BLYPP1267L).</p>

    <p>hereinafter referred to as the &lsquo;Borrower (s)&rsquo;, which term shall unless repugnant to the context shall mean and include his/her heirs, representatives, successors, executors, attorneys, administrators and assigns, of the party at the &lsquo;First Part&rsquo;.</p>

    <p class="center">AND</p>

    <p><b>M/S. ANANDA HOMES (GST No: 36ABFFA6591E1ZE)</b>, a partnership Company incorporated under the provisions of the Companies Act, 1956, having its Registered Office at Plot No. 17 &amp; 18, Dev N Dev Layout, Golden Mile Road, Beside Allu Studios, Kokapet, Hyderabad, Rangareddy, Telangana-500075. by its authorized signatory SRI. P.V. SREENIVASULU S/O. LATE P.C.V. RAMANAIAH, Resident of VillaNo.60, River Edge Villas, Manchirevula, K. V. Ranga Reddy, Telangana &ndash; 500089, which term shall unless repugnant to the context shall mean and include its representatives, successors, administrators and assigns, of the party at the &lsquo;Second Part&rsquo;.</p>

    <p class="center">AND</p>

    <p><b>State Bank of India</b>, a body corporate, constituted under the State Bank of India Act 1955, having amongst others one of its Branch Office at&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;..............</p>

    <p>hereinafter referred as the &lsquo;SBI&rsquo;, which term shall unless repugnant to the context shall mean and include its representatives, successors, administrators and assigns, of the party at the &lsquo;Third Part&rsquo;.</p>

    <p>Whereas, the &lsquo;Builder/Developer&rsquo; is the absolute owner and in peaceful possession of the residential property bearing no. Sy.Nos. 128/1A/2/2, 129/A/1, 129/A/2, 129/AA/1, 129/AA/2, 129/AA/3, 129/E/1, 130/A/1, 130/A/2, 130/A/3/1, 130/A/3/2, 130/A/4, 130/AA/1, 130/AA/2, 130/AA/3, 130/E/1, 130/E/2, 145/1/2, 145/1/1/7, 145/1/1/1/2, 145/1/1/1/1/2, 145/1/1/1/1/1/1, 145/1/1/1/1/1/2, 145/2, 147/A/1, 147/A/2, 147/A/3, 147/AA/1, 147/AA/2, 147/AA/3, 147/E/1, 147/E/2, 148/A/1, 148/A/2, 148/A/3, 148/A/4, 148/AA/1, 148/AA/2, 148/AA/3, 148/E/1, 148/E/2, 148/E/3, 148/E/5, 149/1, 149/2, 149/3, 149/4, 149/5, 149/6, 149/7,, situated at Puppalguda Village, under Manikonda Municipality, Gandipet Mandal, Ranga Reddy District, Telangana State and whereas HMDA has sanctioned building plan vide 01722/SKP/Plg/HMDA/2022 dated:25/06/2024. to construct a residential apartment on the said property. Whereas &lsquo;Builder&rsquo; has taken up construction of residential apartment known as &ldquo;THE LEGACEY&rdquo; on the said property.</p>

    <p>Whereas, the party at the second part has registered the said real estate project namely&rdquo; THE LEGACEY&rdquo; (hereinafter referred to as the Project) with the Real Estate Regulatory Authority (RERA) / Telangana Real Estate Regulatory Authority (TSRERA) of TELANGANA and been granted registration number P02400008615, dated:07/08/2024. which is valid and subsisting as on date.</p>

    <p>Whereas, the Party at the Second Part shall complete the construction of the flats latest by December,2029. And is booking the sale of the unit/apartment. The proposed buyer has to make the payment of the Sale Consideration and other charges, if any, by 31/12/2027 and on the payment of the entire consideration, the Party at the Second Part shall hand over the possession of the flat to the said proposed buyer.</p>

    <p>Whereas, the Party at the First Part has booked a flat bearing No. T2-1508 (EAST Facing) on 15th Floor, of Tower-2, the High-Rise Residential Flats known as &ldquo;THE LEGACEY&rdquo;, with saleable area of 1825 Square Feet (including common areas and One Car Parking), along with proportionate undivided share of land equivalent to 38.3 Square Yards. in the building which the Party at the Second Part shall construct on the above said Flat and the Party at the First Part has to pay the entire consideration amount by Rs. 1,46,55,375/- (Rupeers One Crore Forty-Six Lakh Fifty-Five Thousand Three Hundred and Seventy-Five) Including GST.</p>

    <p>Whereas, the Party at the First Part has approached the Party at the Third Part for availing a Home Loan of Rs....................................... (Rupees &hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;&hellip;........................................only) to finance the purchase of the said flat. Besides other securities, the Party at the First Part has agreed to create the charge over the said flat along with the proportionate undivided share in the land in favour of the Party at the Third Part. In the absence of proper Conveyance Deed/Sale Deed in its favour, the Party at the First Part is not in a position to create a valid mortgage over the said flat and proportionate share of land in favour of the Party at the Third Part.</p>

    <p>Whereas, the Party at the First Part and the Party at the Second Part have requested SBI to disburse the said loan to the Borrower, notwithstanding the fact that the Conveyance Deed/Sale Deed is not executed in favour of the Party at the First Part at this stage, and in consideration of the SBI sanctioning the loan to the Borrower(s), the Borrower(s) and the Builder/Developer have executed this Agreement on the following terms and conditions.</p>

    <p class="heading">Now therefore it is hereby agreed by and between the parties that:</p>

    <p>1. The SBI has and shall have the first lien over the said flat for the due repayment of the loan which SBI has granted to the Borrower. The Builder shall note in its records the charge and lien of SBI over the said flat. The Builder shall not transfer the said flat to any other person without the prior written consent of the SBI.</p>

    <p>2. The Builder/Developer agrees that it has no objection to the Borrower(s) mortgaging the said flat with proportionate share in land to the SBI as security for the said loan agreed to be advanced by the SBI for the purpose of purchase / construction of the said flat. In the event of default in the repayment of loan and/ or the Borrower(s) committing any other default which makes the Borrower(s) liable for the repayment of the entire amount outstanding in the said loan as per the terms of the Loan Agreement executed between the Borrower(s) and the SBI, the Builder shall at the request of SBI, be under obligation to not deliver possession to the Borrower and/or to cancel the booking. Further, Builder shall pay all amounts received by the Builder from SBI on behalf of the Borrower(s) alongwith accrued interest on home loan account or amount received on behalf of the Borrower(s) including also any amount paid by the Borrower to the Builder whichever is lower within the period of 90 days from the effective date of request by SBI. However, in case the Builder/Developer fails to refund the amount, the Builder/Developer shall be liable to pay the total amount alongwith interest @ EBLR of SBI plus 2% over the said amount. Upon payment of the amounts by the Builder/Developer to SBI as aforesaid, the SBI and the Borrower will not have any claim, charge, lien, mortgage, right, title and interest etc. whatsoever, over the said flat. SBI shall issue a certificate to release any mortgage/charge/lien created on the said flat. Borrower hereby expressly agrees that in the event of default in either repayment of the loan or any other default by the Borrower, SBI shall be entitled to request the Builder to cancel the booking and return the amounts received by the Builder and the Borrower agrees and acknowledges that any such request by SBI and payment made by the Builder under this clause to SBI shall be binding upon the Borrower.</p>

    <p>3. That if for any reason there is any increase/escalation in the cost of the said flat, the increase shall be paid and borne by the Borrower(s) without any reference to the SBI and until such payment is made, the SBI shall have the right to suspend further disbursement of the said loan.</p>

    <p>4. That the agreement for sale is already entered into by the borrower and the Builder/Developer and duly registered or shall be entered into by the borrower and Builder/Developer and duly registered as per standard format of TS RERA (state RERA rules to be mentioned of the state where the project is under progress). The said registered agreement for sale is/shall be delivered to the bank.</p>

    <p>(Wherever registration of agreement for sale is not mandatory under Registration Act as applicable in the State / RERA provisions, this clause will not be applicable. In case registration is not mandatory, the un-registered sale agreement shall be delivered to the Bank).</p>

    <p>5. That the Builder/Developer and borrower agree that they shall comply with the provisions of Real Estate Regulation &amp; Development Act,2016 and TS RERA (state RERA rules to be mentioned of the state where the project is under progress). The Builder/Developer and borrower agree that they shall inform the Bank immediately upon suspension or revocation of registration of the project under the said Act. In the event of the borrower claiming any amount including but not limited to refund of amount paid with interest or compensation or interest for delay from the Builder/Developer under the above Act for any reason, the Builder/Developer shall make payment of such amount directly to the Bank and the borrower agrees that such payment to the Bank shall be binding on him and deemed to be a discharge of his liability to the extent of the money so paid to the Bank. Further, the borrower shall be liable for interest, if any, payable to the Builder/Developer under the above Act for any reason whatsoever.</p>

    <p>6. That in the event of the Builder cancelling the said booking for any default committed by the Borrower(s) or the project is shelved by the Builder or for any other reason whatsoever, the Builder shall pay, all amounts received by the Builder from SBI on behalf of the Borrower(s) along with accrued interest on home loan account OR, any amount received on behalf of the Borrower(s) from the Bank including the amount paid by the Borrower directly to the Builder, whichever is lower, within the period of 90 days from the effective date of request by SBI. However, the builder/developer shall be entitled to recover cancellation and/or any other charges, if any payable by the Borrower under the terms of application form for purchase of the said flat and/or agreement to sell/construction out of the surplus available if any after full recovery of bank&rsquo;s dues only in the instance where the Borrower has cancelled the booking of the flat or has committed any default.</p>

    <p>7. That on the receipt of the entire consideration amount and other dues payable by the borrower/purchaser as per Agreement for sale/allotment letter, the Builder/Developer shall execute a proper Conveyance Deed/Sale Deed/Lease Deed in favour of the Borrower. The Builder undertakes to deliver the same along with original registration fee receipt directly to the SBI and not to the Borrower(s). Before the execution of the Sale Deed/Conveyance Deed/Lease Deed, the builder shall inform the SBI about the same on the completion of the project.</p>

    <p>8. That the builder agrees that the loan amount may be credited to the loan account no.</p>

    <p>That the builder agrees that the loan Flat amount may be credited to the Escrow account</p>

